From 56760b37b8412c54aec5174b3e64e5b0826629ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RexxColder <palettafacundo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:00:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] VIF1/VU1 on its own thread; faster VU1 pipeline model;
 VU1 record/replay check

- PS2Memory runs VIF1 DMA transfers on a worker thread (PS2X_VIF1_THREAD=0 keeps
  them inline). The EE waits for it before touching VIF/GIF registers and FIFOs,
  VU1 memory, GS privileged registers, GIF/VIF0 DMA or the GS from HLE stubs, and
  applies the completion (STR, D_STAT, DMAC handlers) on its own thread.
  GS SIGNAL/FINISH raised by a worker transfer are held and raised before that
  transfer's DMAC completion: queued after it, Downhill Jam drew broken text.
  PS2X_VIF1_STATS=1 reports jobs and EE wait time.
- VU1 interpreter: valid-entry bit masks for every pipeline (commit visits only
  live entries), FMAC flag classification in double with a long double fallback
  only for results that round to FLT_MAX. Results are bit-identical.
- PS2X_VU1_RECORD=<dir> (PS2X_VU1_RECORD_COUNT, PS2X_VU1_RECORD_EVERY) saves the
  VU1 state and memories at MSCAL/MSCNT; ps2x_vu1_replay re-runs them and prints a
  hash of registers, data memory, XGKICK packets and cycles, to check interpreter
  changes against a reference. VU1Interpreter::setPacketSink receives XGKICKs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
